ed to ____ for help.","options":["call","sweep","cook","iron"],"answer":0,"explain":"Loud signals attract attention."},{"q":"If you get lost in a market, ____.","options":["stay put and look for a security post / tell a seller with a stall to find police","hide in a boot of a car","leave town","follow any stranger home"],"answer":0,"explain":"Stay visible and ask official help."},{"q":"Bullying should be ____.","options":["praised","reported","copied","kept as a secret always"],"answer":1,"explain":"Tell a teacher."},{"q":"Do not play with ____.","options":["a football in a field","puzzles","story books","fire and matches"],"answer":3,"explain":"Fire can burn."},{"q":"If a stranger asks you to go with them, you should ____.","options":["follow quietly","say no and tell an adult","keep it secret","enter the car"],"answer":1,"explain":"Never go with a stranger."},{"q":"Security education teaches us to stay ____.","options":["away from school","silent in class always","afraid of everyone forever","safe"],"answer":3,"explain":"Be alert, not fearful."},{"q":"The assembly point is where we ____ in an emergency.","options":["buy snacks","play football first","hide from teachers","meet"],"answer":3,"explain":"Schools have assembly points."},{"q":"Medicines at home should be kept ____.","options":["out of children’s reach","in drink bottles","on the floor","next to sweets"],"answer":0,"explain":"Wrong medicine is dangerous."},{"q":"The police emergency number often taught is ____.","options":["7777","0000","199","12"],"answer":2,"explain":"199 can reach the police."},{"q":"Do not take ____ given by friends without an adult’s knowledge.","options":["unknown drugs or tablets","your own lunch","your own water bottle","a textbook"],"answer":0,"explain":"Unknown substances can harm you."},{"q":"In a stampede, move ____ the crowd if you can, protect your chest.","options":["deeper into","against blindly","sideways out of","by sitting in the middle"],"answer":2,"explain":"Protect yourself; don’t push."},{"q":"When the alarm rings, ____.","options":["lock yourself in the toilet always","run in any direction screaming only","ignore it","follow emergency instructions"],"answer":3,"explain":"Practise drills seriously."},{"q":"School ID and visitors’ passes help to ____.","options":["know who belongs","decorate only","cook","play football"],"answer":0,"explain":"Visitors should report at the gate."},{"q":"Flood safety: do not walk in ____ water.","options":["a puddle with an adult on the compound","a shallow known gutter at home never anyway wait","a bath","fast or deep"],"answer":3,"explain":"Flood water can hide holes and germs."},{"q":"Cyber predators may pretend to be ____.","options":["your parent at home","your head teacher in person","children or friends","the school bell"],"answer":2,"explain":"Never meet an online stranger alone."},{"q":"When cycling, wear a ____.","options":["helmet","blindfold","long loose scarf in the wheel","earphones at full volume always"],"answer":0,"explain":"Helmets protect the head."},{"q":"If you are in danger, tell a ____ adult.","options":["unknown online only","nobody","a stray animal","trusted"],"answer":3,"explain":"Parents, teachers and police can help."},{"q":"Do not take gifts from ____.","options":["your parents","strangers","your teacher as a prize","grandparents"],"answer":1,"explain":"Strangers may not be safe."},{"q":"Your body is private. If someone touches you in a bad way, ____.","options":["keep silent forever","hide at the market","blame yourself","tell a trusted adult"],"answer":3,"explain":"It is not your fault. Speak up."},{"q":"Online, do not share your ____.","options":["favourite subject","first name only with teacher","address and password","class"],"answer":2,"explain":"Personal data can be misused."},{"q":"Which is a safe action?","options":["sharing your password","following a stranger","opening unknown links","telling a teacher about bullying"],"answer":3,"explain":"That action help